 C/TF:,NAME,DTRAN  /01.06.84/    . Truncate (rewrite) a file
C===========================================================
C C/TF - truncate file (= rewrite).  Empties the buffer and
C  re-initialises the packed-mode state so a fresh write run
C  can begin.  The tail walks the [M1+37B] track-table, reading
C  each entry via `1,WTC,37B' (no patching - WTC just uses
C  [M1+37B] as the next instruction's address operand).
C
C C/OI - open an input file: move FILE[3] into FILE[5] and
C  release the track chain hanging off it.
C
C C/CB - close the current buffer window: reset FILE[19] and
C  FILE[0] to FILE[12], and FILE[0] to FILE[13] when packed.
C  Returns through M14.
C
C  Labelled in p_sys.asm: C/TF = OUTFIN, C/OI = OPENIN,
C  C/CB = CLOSEWIN.
C===========================================================
C Register convention (see FILE.md):
C   M12 = base of the FILE record being acted on
C   M1  = runtime constant table ([M1+8] = 1U, [M1+9] = integer-tag
C         mask, [M1+12] = positive-mantissa mask, [M1+25B] = MSB;
C         [M1+3..5] and [M1+35B..37B] are runtime scratch)
C   M13 = link register set by the calling VJM
C   M14 = secondary link (used inside packed-mode helpers)
 PASLANE*:,LC,1              . 0o76000 buffer/lane mask
 C/AD:,SUBP,                 . advance the file buffer iterator
 C/CB:,SUBP,                 . forward decl, defined below
 C/OI:,SUBP,                 . forward decl, defined below
 C/ZI:,SUBP,                 . declared to pull PASCTRP into the load:
C  it owns the load-time seed for PASLANE*, and this is the only
C  user that does not otherwise call into that module.
 14,VJM,C/CB                 . close any open window first
 ,XTA,
 12,ATX,11B                  . FILE[9]  := 0
 12,ATX,12B                  . FILE[10] := 0
 ,UTC,PASLANE*               . C := address of lane mask
 ,XTA,
 12,ATX,6                    . FILE[6]  := lane mask
 14,VJM,C/AD
 1,XTA,10B
 12,ATX,2                    . FILE[2]  := 1U (pending write)
 12,ATX,16B                  . FILE[14] := 1U
 12,XTA,4
 ,U1A,INPFILE
 ,UJ,C/OI
 INPFILE:,XTA,               . input file: just clear FILE[5]
 12,ATX,5
 13,UJ,
 C/OI:,ENTRY,
 12,XTA,3                    . output: load FILE[3] (track id)
 13,UZA,                     . zero -> just return
 12,ATX,5                    . FILE[5] := FILE[3]
 TRKLOOP:12,WTC,5            . loop: WT := FILE[5]
 ,XTA,
 ,U1A,NEXTTRK                . non-zero -> NEXTTRK
 1,XTA,37B                   . [M1+31] := track id
 12,WTC,5
 ,ATX,                       . store zero into the track header
 12,XTA,3
 1,ATX,37B                   . [M1+31] := FILE[3]
 ,XTA,
 12,ATX,3                    . FILE[3] := 0
 12,ATX,5                    . FILE[5] := 0
 13,UJ,                      . return
 NEXTTRK:12,ATX,5            . FILE[5] := non-zero scan word
 ,UJ,TRKLOOP
C---------------------------------------------------------------
 C/CB:,ENTRY,
 12,XTA,14B
 12,ATX,23B                  . FILE[19] := FILE[12]
 12,ATX,                     . FILE[0]  := FILE[12]
 12,XTA,22B
 14,UZA,                     . text -> return via M14
 12,XTA,15B                  . else also reset FILE[1] window
 12,ATX,
 14,UJ,
 ,END,
